   "fix": "Drop `hab` and case-split inside: `rcases le_or_gt b a` with the degenerate branch `simp [uniformMeasure_eq_zero_of_le hba, Set.Ioc_eq_empty_of_le hba]`. Then `ContinuousOn.integrable_uniformMeasure` (lines 59-64) loses its own case split and becomes a one-liner.",
   "issue": "`integrable_uniformMeasure_iff` assumes `hab : a < b`, but the iff holds for every pair of endpoints: for `b \u2264 a`, `uniformMeasure a b = 0` (TauCeti `uniformMeasure_eq_zero_of_le`) and `Set.Ioc a b = \u2205`, so both sides are `Integrable f 0`, true by Mathlib's `integrable_zero_measure` (Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Function/L1Space/Integrable.lean:283). The hypothesis is only needed by the chosen proof (`integrable_smul_measure` wants a nonzero, finite scalar).",
   "line": 51
  }
